     mmppee — MPLS Provider Edge

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ppsseeuuddoo--ddeevviiccee mmppee

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmppee interface is a Multiprotocol Label Switching (MPLS) Provider Edge
     pseudo-device used to enter and leave an MPLS domain.

     An mmppee interface can be created at runtime using the iiffccoonnffiigg mmppee_N ccrreeaattee
     command or by setting up a hostname.if(5) configuration file for
     netstart(8).  The interface itself can be configured with ifconfig(8);
     see its manual page for more information.

IIOOCCTTLLSS
     The following ioctl(2) calls are specific to mmppee, mpip(4) and mpw(4) in‐
     terfaces:

        SIOCSETLABEL  Encapsulate packets entering this interface in MPLS us‐
                      ing the specified label.

        SIOCGETLABEL  Report the label that packets entering this interface
                      will be tagged with.

        SIOCDELLABEL  Unset the MPLS label.

